{"command": "cd /testbed && head -45 specs/001-transactions/data-model.md && echo ===QUICKSTART=== && cat specs/001-transactions/quickstart.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "# Phase 1 Data Model: Atomic Batch Transactions for TinyDB\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17\n\n## Entities\n\n### Operation\nA single unit of batch work (spec §Key Entities).\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation |\n|-------|------|----------|------------|\n| `op` | `str` | yes | exactly `'insert'` or `'remove'` |\n| `document` | `Mapping` (dict) | for `op='insert'` | must be a Mapping; `bool` rejected; nested structures allowed |\n| `doc_id` | `int` | for `op='remove'` | must be `int` (not `bool`) and `> 0` |\n\n- Entry must be a `dict`; otherwise `ValueError`.\n- Extra keys are ignored (research R4).\n- State: immutable input — the writer never mutates the caller's operation dict (R03).\n\n### Batch\nAn ordered `list[Operation]`.\n\n- Empty list is valid → `apply([])` returns `[]`, no state change.\n- Applied as a unit: all effects persist, or none do (R02).\n- Output: `list[int]` of inserted document IDs in submission order; removes contribute nothing.\n\n### Document\nA JSON-like mapping stored in the default table, identified by a positive integer ID.\n\n- ID assignment: done by the existing `Table` machinery (`_get_next_id`), **not** by the writer; IDs are never caller-chosen (spec §Assumptions).\n- Nested dicts/lists are stored as deep copies (R03; research R3).\n- Read back through the Table API as fresh `Document` objects — no aliasing with storage or caller data.\n\n### Default table (scope boundary)\n\n- The single table the writer touches, accessed via `db.table('_default')`.\n- Raw shape in storage: `dict[str, dict[int, Mapping]]` under the `'_default'` key of the whole-database state `dict[str, dict[str, Any]]` (observed `Storage.read/write` signatures).\n- **Snapshot**: `deepcopy` of the raw `'_default'` table dict taken before any mutation; the only state the writer keeps between the start and end of a batch.\n- Other tables: never read, written, or snapshotted.\n\n## Relationships\n\n- `BatchWriter 1──N Operation` (one batch = ordered list).\n- `Operation 1──1 Document` (insert) or `Operation 1──1 doc_id` (remove).\n- `Document N──1 Default table`.\n===QUICKSTART===\n# Quickstart / Validation Guide: Atomic Batch Transactions for TinyDB\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17\n\nThis is a validation/run guide. It proves the feature works end-to-end; it does not contain implementation code. API details: [contracts/batch-writer.md](contracts/batch-writer.md). Data shapes: [data-model.md](data-model.md).\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3.12 (observed `python3 --version` → `Python 3.12.14`).\n- Repository root `/testbed`; the package is importable from the root (`python3 -c \"import tinydb\"` → `/testbed/tinydb/__init__.py`).\n- pytest is installed; **pytest-cov is NOT** installed, so always override the repo's `pytest.ini` addopts with `-o addopts=\"\"` (evidence: `python3 -m pytest -o addopts=\"\" tests/test_utils.py -q` → `12 passed`).\n\n## Setup (implementation phase)\n\n1. Create `tinydb/journal.py` with `BatchWriter` per the contract.\n2. Create `tests/test_journal.py` covering T01–T12 from the contract's Test Mapping.\n3. Do **not** modify `acceptance_public.py`, `tests/` upstream files, or any existing `tinydb/` module.\n\n## Validation Scenarios\n\n### S1 — Public acceptance gate (R01 + R02 core)\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed && python3 -m pytest -o addopts=\"\" acceptance_public.py -v\n```\n\n**Expected**: `test_public_basic` and `test_public_atomic` both PASS. Before implementation this command fails collection with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tinydb.journal'` (observed) — passing after implementation is the primary end-to-end proof.\n\n### S2 — Own test suite (R01–R03 full coverage)\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed && python3 -m pytest -o addopts=\"\" tests/test_journal.py -v\n```\n\n**Expected**: all T01–T12 scenarios pass, including: empty batch `[]`; insert ID ordering; every malformed-op `ValueError`; rollback restoring the complete pre-batch table (T05/T06); pre-acquired handle visibility after success and rollback (T07); ID sequencing after rollback (T08); ordinary API transparency (T09); no-aliasing of nested data (T10); duplicate-remove failure (T11); other tables untouched (T12).\n\n### S3 — Upstream regression gate (Constitution I)\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed && python3 -m pytest -o addopts=\"\" tests/ -q\n```\n\n**Expected**: the full unchanged upstream suite passes (baseline before implementation, recorded 2026-10-17: `223 passed in 1.28s`; after implementation: same count, no failures).\n\n### S4 — Manual smoke check (no-aliasing, R03)\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\nfrom tinydb.storages import MemoryStorage\nfrom tinydb.journal import BatchWriter\n\ndb = TinyDB(storage=MemoryStorage)\nw = BatchWriter(db)\nop = {'op': 'insert', 'document': {'nested': {'a': [1, 2]}}}\nids = w.apply([op])\nassert ids == [1], ids\nop['document']['nested']['a'].append(99)          # mutate caller input\ndoc = db.get(doc_id=1)\nassert doc['nested']['a'] == [1, 2], doc          # DB unaffected\ndoc['nested']['a'].append(7)                      # mutate returned doc\nassert db.get(doc_id=1)['nested']['a'] == [1, 2]  # still unaffected\nprint('S4 OK')\nPY\n```\n\n**Expected**: prints `S4 OK`.\n\n### S5 — Rollback with a pre-acquired handle (R02)\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\nfrom tinydb.storages import MemoryStorage\nfrom tinydb.journal import BatchWriter\n\ndb = TinyDB(storage=MemoryStorage)\nt = db.table('_default')          # pre-acquired handle\ndb.insert({'x': 1})\ntry:\n    w = BatchWriter(db)\n    w.apply([{'op': 'insert', 'document': {'x': 2}},\n             {'op': 'remove', 'doc_id': 99}])\n    raise SystemExit('expected ValueError')\nexcept ValueError:\n    pass\nassert [d['x'] for d in t.all()] == [1], t.all()  # handle sees rollback\nids = BatchWriter(db).apply([{'op': 'insert', 'document': {'x': 3}}])\nassert ids == [2] and [d['x'] for d in t.all()] == [1, 3]\nprint('S5 OK')\nPY\n```\n\n**Expected**: prints `S5 OK` (rollback visible through the old handle; next ID after rollback is `2`, no reuse of the rolled-back ID).\n\n## Done Criteria (phase gate evidence)\n\n- S1 passes (record command + output).\n- S2 passes (record command + output).\n- S3 passes with the same result as the pre-implementation baseline (record both).\n- S4 and S5 print `OK`.\n- `git status --short` shows no modifications to upstream `tests/`, `acceptance_public.py`, or existing `tinydb/` modules (only new `tinydb/journal.py`, `tests/test_journal.py`, and spec artifacts).\n"}